1
00:00:11,719 --> 00:00:15,181
Absolutely. Sir, I'll let you know
as soon as I know anything.

2
00:00:15,806 --> 00:00:18,017
Not at all. It's... It's my pleasure.

3
00:00:18,809 --> 00:00:20,186
- Crap.
- Director?

4
00:00:20,728 --> 00:00:24,398
Bertram wants regular updates. Somebody
involved in this case must be connected.

5
00:00:24,857 --> 00:00:26,609
Well, maybe we'll get lucky, catch a dunk.

6
00:00:26,734 --> 00:00:29,153
- We're due an easy one.
- Ugh, you shouldn't have said that.

7
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,697
- Said what?
- "We're due an easy one".

8
00:00:32,031 --> 00:00:33,074
Now we're jinxed.

9
00:00:33,407 --> 00:00:34,450
Sorry.

10
00:00:37,453 --> 00:00:40,498
Amber Sutherland, documentary filmmaker.
The house is a rental.

11
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:42,166
She's been in Crane Creek
for about two months

12
00:00:42,291 --> 00:00:44,377
making a campaign video
for mayor Kenyon Bagshaw.

13
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:46,337
Isn't a campaign video overkill
for a small town mayor?

14
00:00:46,462 --> 00:00:47,505
Well, Bagshaw's moving up.

15
00:00:47,713 --> 00:00:49,966
He's running in a special election
for the house of representatives.

16
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:51,300
Surprise. Connected.

17
00:00:51,425 --> 00:00:54,220
Agent Lisbon? Chief Arnold Nail,
Crane Creek P.D.

18
00:00:54,512 --> 00:00:57,515
My men responded to a shots-fired
call last night, found the body.

19
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:59,559
- Agent Cho, Agent Rigsby.
- Men.

20
00:00:59,767 --> 00:01:00,810
Did your men search the area?

21
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:03,479
We found a .38 in a trash can
down the street.

22
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:05,481
Serial number shows it reported stolen

23
00:01:05,606 --> 00:01:07,358
from a man one town over
about a year ago.

24
00:01:07,483 --> 00:01:09,110
- We're gonna need that.
- Got it.

25
00:01:09,902 --> 00:01:12,029
And just so you know, I get it.

26
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,198
CBI's in charge.
We're here to assist.

27
00:01:14,323 --> 00:01:16,242
Thanks, chief.
We don't always get a welcome.

28
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:18,953
Well, I said I get it.
I didn't say I liked it.

29
00:01:19,161 --> 00:01:21,163
Looks like the killer tossed the place.
Anything missing?

30
00:01:21,455 --> 00:01:23,833
Apparently, Amber had a lotta
high-end video equipment.

31
00:01:24,208 --> 00:01:26,294
There's no sign of it,
so we figure the killer took it.

32
00:01:26,627 --> 00:01:27,670
Robbery gone bad?

33
00:01:27,795 --> 00:01:29,505
No, there's a lot of other valuables
left behind.

34
00:01:30,006 --> 00:01:31,340
Okay, get a list of what's missing

35
00:01:31,507 --> 00:01:33,759
and call Jane and ask him
why he isn't here already.

36
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,396
Patrick Jane, CBI.
I'm on the way to a crime scene.

37
00:01:46,355 --> 00:01:47,898
Do you know how fast
you were going, sir?

38
00:01:48,232 --> 00:01:49,859
Do I get a prize if I guess correctly?

39
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:52,445
13 miles per hour
over the posted speed limit.

40
00:01:53,362 --> 00:01:55,072
I need your license
and proof of insurance.

41
00:01:55,364 --> 00:01:57,908
I'd love to, but, uh, we got
a murder to solve.

42
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:00,578
Evidence degrading,
killers perfecting their alibis.

43
00:02:00,703 --> 00:02:02,288
First 48 hours...
You know that, right?

44
00:02:02,413 --> 00:02:04,165
License and proof of insurance.

45
00:02:05,666 --> 00:02:07,251
I mean, is this really necessary?

46
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:09,670
Aren't we all part of the Justice League?

47
00:02:09,795 --> 00:02:12,048
Do you think Aquaman
would give Batman a ticket?

48
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:15,384
Just consider that.

49
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:18,137
Step out of the car.

50
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:25,603
There's no sign of a struggle.
She probably knew the killer.

51
00:02:25,853 --> 00:02:27,980
But if it was personal,
why take her video equipment?

52
00:02:28,397 --> 00:02:30,232
Agent Lisbon, we might have something.

53
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:33,527
One of my officers is engaged
in a pursuit off a traffic stop.

54
00:02:33,778 --> 00:02:35,112
Driver was acting crazy.

55
00:02:35,946 --> 00:02:38,282
- Could be our guy.
- Don't say a word.

56
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:43,037
Vehicle is a blue Citroen,
about 30 years old

57
00:02:43,454 --> 00:02:44,538
California plates.

58
00:02:44,997 --> 00:02:46,082
See what you did?

59
00:02:51,879 --> 00:02:53,130
"Pull over!"

60
00:02:59,553 --> 00:03:02,640
- Morning, Lisbon.
- Freeze! Let me see your hands!

61
00:03:03,891 --> 00:03:04,934
Did I miss anything?

62
00:03:20,114 --> 00:03:23,742
Agent, I'm not opposed to extending
professional courtesy

63
00:03:24,243 --> 00:03:27,705
but your man ignored a reasonable request
from my officer and fled.

64
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:29,248
- He will pay the ticket.
- Meh.

65
00:03:29,623 --> 00:03:32,876
Speed traps. Legalized extortion.
You want people to slow down?

66
00:03:33,085 --> 00:03:34,962
Park out in the open,
where they can see you.

67
00:03:35,087 --> 00:03:37,756
But no, you lay in wait
like thieves in the night.

68
00:03:37,923 --> 00:03:39,925
- He will pay the ticket today.
- I'm not gonna pay it.

69
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:42,136
- Jane! Stop... stop that.
- I won't pay it. I'm not paying it.

70
00:03:42,261 --> 00:03:43,595
Extortionist.

71
00:03:43,929 --> 00:03:47,975
{\an8}If Mr. Jane will go to City Hall
and settle this today

72
00:03:48,225 --> 00:03:49,643
- we can move on.
- Thank you.

73
00:03:49,935 --> 00:03:51,895
- I'd like an apology.
- Oh, really?

74
00:03:52,187 --> 00:03:54,189
Dream bigger, pal.
You're not gonna get one from me.

75
00:03:54,815 --> 00:03:56,692
{\an8}I said we'd move on.

76
00:03:59,445 --> 00:04:00,738
Yes, we're moving on.

77
00:04:01,905 --> 00:04:04,116
{\an8}Don't know why you were in such
an all-fired hurry to get here.

78
00:04:06,201 --> 00:04:07,453
I'll tell you who killed that woman.

79
00:04:07,911 --> 00:04:08,954
Who's that?

80
00:04:09,079 --> 00:04:11,081
{\an8}Local scumbag
named Ronald Crosswhite.

81
00:04:11,707 --> 00:04:13,083
{\an8}Killed his wife two years ago.

82
00:04:13,292 --> 00:04:15,502
{\an8}He was indicted for murdering his wife.

83
00:04:15,627 --> 00:04:17,546
- Oh, he did it, all right.
- Sergeant Rowley!

84
00:04:18,839 --> 00:04:19,882
Why isn't he in prison?

85
00:04:22,426 --> 00:04:24,428
There was a... screw-up.

86
00:04:24,678 --> 00:04:26,889
Evidentiary paperwork got filed late.

87
00:04:27,389 --> 00:04:30,768
Judge excluded some security footage.
Critical evidence.

88
00:04:31,518 --> 00:04:32,728
Crosswhite walked.

89
00:04:34,146 --> 00:04:35,189
Aha.

90
00:04:37,149 --> 00:04:38,317
And you're the one that screwed up.

91
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:42,154
That's why you can't stop looking
at that poor woman's body

92
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:43,655
because you feel responsible.

93
00:04:45,866 --> 00:04:47,785
{\an8}Also explains why
when there's a murder in town

94
00:04:47,951 --> 00:04:49,495
{\an8}you're out working the speed trap.

95
00:04:50,746 --> 00:04:52,915
- You smart-ass.
- Stand down. Now.

96
00:04:55,459 --> 00:04:56,502
Yeah.

97
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:59,671
{\an8}Looks like we both have a little problem
controlling our underlings.

98
00:04:59,797 --> 00:05:02,424
{\an8}- Underling?
- Even if Crosswhite did kill his wife

99
00:05:02,549 --> 00:05:04,927
{\an8}what does that have to do
with Amber Sutherland?

100
00:05:06,762 --> 00:05:09,223
{\an8}Saw the two of 'em together
day before yesterday.

101
00:05:10,015 --> 00:05:11,058
{\an8}Now she's dead.

102
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:13,060
{\an8}No way that's a coincidence.

103
00:05:14,728 --> 00:05:16,063
Underling? Really?

104
00:05:16,188 --> 00:05:17,314
Lisbon, would you explain
to this man...

105
00:05:17,439 --> 00:05:19,316
{\an8}- You need to stop.
- I'm... I'm a consultant.

106
00:05:19,441 --> 00:05:21,318
{\an8}- He's a consultant.
- I'm not below or above.

107
00:05:21,443 --> 00:05:23,445
- I am to the side.
- That's enough.

108
00:05:27,699 --> 00:05:31,620
{\an8}Ginger Crosswhite was 31.
Worked at City Hall, DMV clerk.

109
00:05:31,787 --> 00:05:34,081
Shot and killed in their living room
two years ago.

110
00:05:34,498 --> 00:05:37,251
{\an8}The D.A. claimed Crosswhite
did it for insurance money.

111
00:05:37,543 --> 00:05:39,628
He had an upholstery shop
that was struggling.

112
00:05:40,546 --> 00:05:42,631
{\an8}- And he walked?
- "Well, Crosswhite claimed"

113
00:05:42,756 --> 00:05:44,550
{\an8}"he came home from a drive
and found the body."

114
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,885
{\an8}"A security camera image
showed him arriving home"

115
00:05:47,010 --> 00:05:49,680
"an hour before he said he got there.
Destroyed his alibi."

116
00:05:49,847 --> 00:05:51,807
{\an8}"But sergeant Rowley missed
the deadline"

117
00:05:51,932 --> 00:05:52,975
{\an8}"to file the search warrant"

118
00:05:53,183 --> 00:05:55,477
the judge excluded it,
and the case collapsed.

119
00:05:55,727 --> 00:05:56,770
"Good work."

120
00:05:56,895 --> 00:05:58,772
{\an8}The mayor's wife is coming in
to the office.

121
00:05:58,939 --> 00:06:00,691
{\an8}Her name's Jessica Bagshaw.

122
00:06:00,899 --> 00:06:03,527
{\an8}She was supervising
Amber Sutherland's video work.

123
00:06:03,777 --> 00:06:05,988
- I'll get her statement.
- "Okay. Be careful."

124
00:06:06,154 --> 00:06:07,197
{\an8}They have a lotta pull.

125
00:06:07,698 --> 00:06:09,700
{\an8}Teresa Lisbon,
toughest gal west of the Pecos

126
00:06:09,825 --> 00:06:12,452
{\an8}and you're scared of a small town
mayor and his wife.

127
00:06:20,669 --> 00:06:21,712
Yeah?

128
00:06:21,837 --> 00:06:23,297
Mr. Crosswhite, we're with the CBI.

129
00:06:23,422 --> 00:06:25,757
- I'm Agent Teresa Lisbon.
- And I'm Patrick Jane.

130
00:06:26,174 --> 00:06:28,385
We wanna ask you some questions
about Amber Sutherland.

131
00:06:28,802 --> 00:06:30,095
Tom Rowley tell you about me?

132
00:06:30,721 --> 00:06:31,763
Yes, he did.

133
00:06:32,055 --> 00:06:33,223
That's my buddy Tom.

134
00:06:35,517 --> 00:06:36,560
Can we come in?

135
00:06:39,146 --> 00:06:40,230
How did you know Amber?

136
00:06:42,232 --> 00:06:43,525
She, um...

137
00:06:45,652 --> 00:06:48,739
She was filming me for a documentary.

138
00:06:49,156 --> 00:06:50,198
The one about the mayor?

139
00:06:50,574 --> 00:06:52,701
No, this was about my wife's death.

140
00:06:54,536 --> 00:06:55,579
What are you doing?

141
00:06:55,871 --> 00:06:58,665
Your wife looked lovely.
She had a very gentle face.

142
00:06:58,957 --> 00:07:00,000
Put that down.

143
00:07:00,542 --> 00:07:02,628
- Why?
- Just put it down.

144
00:07:03,462 --> 00:07:04,504
Fair enough.

145
00:07:07,299 --> 00:07:10,469
So Amber was making
a documentary about you?

146
00:07:13,221 --> 00:07:17,017
Yeah. She... she did
a couple interviews.

147
00:07:18,226 --> 00:07:20,354
She said she'd need
to, to raise money to finish it.

148
00:07:20,771 --> 00:07:22,064
That must have been nice for you...

149
00:07:23,190 --> 00:07:24,524
Tell your side to Amber.

150
00:07:26,693 --> 00:07:27,945
You have no idea.

151
00:07:29,446 --> 00:07:32,699
The man who killed my wife
is still out there.

152
00:07:34,618 --> 00:07:36,495
But everyone in town
thinks I'm the killer.

153
00:07:37,537 --> 00:07:39,373
It's, it's around me all the time.

154
00:07:39,790 --> 00:07:41,708
It's like being underwater.

155
00:07:43,293 --> 00:07:44,711
Feels like I can't breathe.

156
00:07:45,629 --> 00:07:47,464
Well, if you didn't kill your wife,
what'd you do to her?

157
00:07:50,217 --> 00:07:51,259
What?

158
00:07:51,510 --> 00:07:53,553
You're the guiltiest-looking man
I've ever seen...

159
00:07:53,679 --> 00:07:54,846
the theatrical squalor

160
00:07:54,972 --> 00:07:57,349
forcing yourself to live
with the hatred of your neighbors.

161
00:07:57,766 --> 00:08:00,602
If you didn't kill your wife,
then why the self-punishment?

162
00:08:02,562 --> 00:08:03,772
You need to get out of here.

163
00:08:05,232 --> 00:08:06,984
- Now.
- I have to agree.

164
00:08:07,275 --> 00:08:08,777
Well, it's just an honest opinion.

165
00:08:09,027 --> 00:08:10,862
A legit question, I'm doing my job.

166
00:08:11,363 --> 00:08:12,990
Okay. Have a nice day.

167
00:08:16,243 --> 00:08:19,621
It just seems insane...
Amber, gone.

168
00:08:21,248 --> 00:08:22,541
She worked closely with you.

169
00:08:22,749 --> 00:08:25,377
She was with us pretty much every day,
the last couple of weeks.

170
00:08:25,627 --> 00:08:27,754
We'll need to speak with your husband,
Mayor Bagshaw.

171
00:08:28,213 --> 00:08:29,256
Of course.

172
00:08:30,048 --> 00:08:31,925
He's forging away on the campaign trail.

173
00:08:32,592 --> 00:08:34,261
Elks clubs and coffee klatches.

174
00:08:35,178 --> 00:08:38,473
Do you have any idea why someone
would wanna hurt Amber?

175
00:08:39,891 --> 00:08:40,976
I can't imagine.

176
00:08:42,477 --> 00:08:44,646
I mean, she was just...

177
00:08:44,938 --> 00:08:47,691
- such a gentle soul.
- Okay.

178
00:08:48,275 --> 00:08:50,944
You know anything about her
personal life? She seeing anybody?

179
00:08:51,486 --> 00:08:55,240
Um, she had been on a few dates
with Zach Gladden.

180
00:08:56,324 --> 00:08:57,367
He works at City Hall.

181
00:08:57,993 --> 00:08:59,327
Was she close with anyone else?

182
00:09:00,537 --> 00:09:01,955
Maybe someone with the campaign?

183
00:09:04,458 --> 00:09:05,792
What is it that you're suggesting?

184
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,920
Nothing. Just...

185
00:09:09,379 --> 00:09:12,966
- She was pretty and...
- And my husband is attractive

186
00:09:13,091 --> 00:09:15,093
and charming and powerful.
Right?

187
00:09:15,677 --> 00:09:18,138
Um, that's not what I was suggesting.

188
00:09:18,263 --> 00:09:20,432
It's how rumors get started.
Um...

189
00:09:21,475 --> 00:09:23,143
We have no interest

190
00:09:23,268 --> 00:09:25,979
in having a pretty dead woman
attached to the campaign

191
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:29,524
if you get my drift, Agent?

192
00:09:30,859 --> 00:09:31,902
Jessica.

193
00:09:32,486 --> 00:09:33,528
Director Bertram.

194
00:09:34,071 --> 00:09:36,156
Gale.
I was gonna come and see you

195
00:09:36,281 --> 00:09:37,949
as soon as Agent Van Pelt
was done with me.

196
00:09:38,158 --> 00:09:39,201
Agent, is she done?

197
00:09:40,452 --> 00:09:41,578
Yes, sir.

198
00:09:42,245 --> 00:09:43,497
Let's grab a cup of coffee.

199
00:10:00,639 --> 00:10:01,681
Zach Gladden?

200
00:10:03,016 --> 00:10:04,101
Tell us about Amber.

201
00:10:04,851 --> 00:10:07,104
I don't know what to say.
She was cool.

202
00:10:08,271 --> 00:10:09,481
God, that's lame.

203
00:10:10,524 --> 00:10:13,151
She was from Los Angeles.
She was funny.

204
00:10:13,944 --> 00:10:16,196
Really hard-working.
Tenacious.

205
00:10:16,446 --> 00:10:17,697
We hear she was spending
some time with a man

206
00:10:17,823 --> 00:10:19,950
named Ronald Crosswhite,
making a documentary?

207
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:22,202
He had been bugging her
since she got into town.

208
00:10:22,536 --> 00:10:25,288
- Someone new to listen to his garbage.
- Garbage, is that how Amber saw it?

209
00:10:25,455 --> 00:10:28,333
She said she was maintaining
her journalistic objectivity.

210
00:10:29,668 --> 00:10:31,837
- Least until a couple of days ago.
- What happened?

211
00:10:32,587 --> 00:10:34,923
She had an interview with him
and she said Crosswhite...

212
00:10:35,423 --> 00:10:36,466
freaked out.

213
00:10:40,762 --> 00:10:41,805
"You okay?"

214
00:10:42,139 --> 00:10:44,891
"Yeah, I guess I'm just...
nervous, you know?"

215
00:10:45,016 --> 00:10:46,101
"Let's start the questions."

216
00:10:46,518 --> 00:10:48,311
Amber e-mailed this video
of the Crosswhite interview

217
00:10:48,436 --> 00:10:49,980
to a producer friend in L.A.
a few days ago.

218
00:10:50,105 --> 00:10:52,566
"Uh, just gotta jump right in, huh?"

219
00:10:52,816 --> 00:10:55,443
"That's right. Your upholstery shop
was still open then."

220
00:10:55,569 --> 00:10:57,362
- This the scary part?
- Wait.

221
00:10:59,739 --> 00:11:02,492
- "There's a discrepancy about the time..."
- "There, there's no discrepancy."

222
00:11:03,034 --> 00:11:04,661
"I've been looking at the security
camera footage..."

223
00:11:04,786 --> 00:11:07,581
"D-d-don't tell me
about s-security footage."

224
00:11:07,831 --> 00:11:09,624
"I was there when I said I was there."

225
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:13,753
"I came home, and my wife was dead.
I mean, don't... don't you get it?"

226
00:11:13,879 --> 00:11:16,047
"There's, there's a real killer
out there somewhere."

227
00:11:16,173 --> 00:11:17,674
- "Okay."
- "You said you believed me."

228
00:11:17,924 --> 00:11:18,967
- "Calm down."
- "Were you lying?"

229
00:11:19,384 --> 00:11:20,844
"Were you lying, too?
Are you one of them?"

230
00:11:21,094 --> 00:11:22,637
- "Please calm down."
- "You one of the... I mean, what is..."

231
00:11:22,762 --> 00:11:24,264
"Don't tell me to calm down!"

232
00:11:24,472 --> 00:11:26,725
- "What is this? What is this, a set-up?
- "I just..."

233
00:11:26,850 --> 00:11:29,102
- "Turn that off! Turn that off!"
- "Please..."

234
00:11:29,352 --> 00:11:30,937
I'll get a warrant first thing
in the morning.

235
00:11:31,104 --> 00:11:33,648
Get a list of Amber's missing equipment
and the serial numbers.

236
00:11:33,815 --> 00:11:34,858
On it.

237
00:11:40,488 --> 00:11:42,908
We're serving a warrant on Crosswhite
first thing in the morning

238
00:11:43,033 --> 00:11:44,075
and you're coming with.

239
00:11:44,784 --> 00:11:46,536
- Oh, sounds like fun.
- Don't worry.

240
00:11:46,661 --> 00:11:48,955
We're dropping you at City Hall
so you can pay that speeding ticket.

241
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:53,835
I thought I made
my feelings very, uh, clear

242
00:11:54,044 --> 00:11:57,297
- on that particular subject...
- Which is why I told chief Nail

243
00:11:57,422 --> 00:11:58,715
if you don't pay it by noon tomorrow

244
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,092
he's free to get a bench warrant
for your arrest.

245
00:12:01,676 --> 00:12:03,511
We're citizens, too.
We're not above the law.

246
00:12:03,887 --> 00:12:06,223
Oh, well, thanks for that, Gandhi.

247
00:12:07,224 --> 00:12:11,061
What I don't appreciate
is this cheap police state tactics.

248
00:12:12,771 --> 00:12:13,855
Whatever works.

249
00:12:17,734 --> 00:12:18,777
He's not here.

250
00:12:19,527 --> 00:12:22,280
Warrant's good either way,
so, Cho, open the door.

251
00:12:33,041 --> 00:12:34,084
Boss.

252
00:12:35,794 --> 00:12:37,045
Found this in the garage.

253
00:12:41,758 --> 00:12:43,551
The serial number matches
Amber's video equipment.

254
00:12:43,677 --> 00:12:46,179
Call Van Pelt, have her put
a BOLO out on Crosswhite.

255
00:12:46,304 --> 00:12:47,347
We need to bring him in.

256
00:12:56,106 --> 00:12:57,482
- Thank you.
- "Good morning, Ms. Bagshaw."

257
00:13:00,527 --> 00:13:02,529
Uh, excuse me, ma'am?
Um, I have a... I have a ticket.

258
00:13:02,654 --> 00:13:03,863
Yes, see that clerk.

259
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:12,330
- So, you're the bagman.
- I guess.

260
00:13:13,290 --> 00:13:16,167
Well, I would like to pay this ticket...

261
00:13:17,294 --> 00:13:19,921
- But under protest.
- Nobody pays any other way.

262
00:13:20,922 --> 00:13:22,382
Everybody stay where they are!

263
00:13:31,973 --> 00:13:33,516
Everybody just stay
right where they are.

264
00:13:33,725 --> 00:13:34,767
Now, you...

265
00:13:35,977 --> 00:13:37,478
you get out there
and lock those front doors.

266
00:13:37,812 --> 00:13:39,564
Try running, you'll have blood
on your hands. Go.

267
00:13:40,982 --> 00:13:43,526
Okay. Okay, ev... everybody over there.

268
00:13:44,027 --> 00:13:45,194
Over there by the window!

269
00:13:47,572 --> 00:13:48,614
Get over there!

270
00:13:51,659 --> 00:13:52,702
Get over there!

271
00:13:58,166 --> 00:13:59,208
Stay there.

272
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,669
Guard, get over here.

273
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,006
Nobody move!

274
00:14:09,552 --> 00:14:11,429
Oh, good. More guns.

275
00:14:18,811 --> 00:14:20,855
Chief. What's going on?

276
00:14:21,606 --> 00:14:23,566
Got a report
Crosswhite's in there with a gun.

277
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,985
- He's got hostages.
- We should secure the perimeter

278
00:14:26,110 --> 00:14:27,612
and make contact with Crosswhite.

279
00:14:28,112 --> 00:14:30,615
Well, thanks for the advice.
My people and I are gonna handle this.

280
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:33,451
You don't wanna start
a gunfight unless you need to.

281
00:14:33,576 --> 00:14:35,244
We should get the information first.

282
00:14:35,411 --> 00:14:36,496
If I'm hearing right

283
00:14:36,746 --> 00:14:39,874
got a group of citizens in there
being threatened by a nut with a gun.

284
00:14:40,375 --> 00:14:41,751
I don't need to know more than that.

285
00:14:46,089 --> 00:14:47,131
Get over there!

286
00:14:47,507 --> 00:14:49,092
Other... other side! Move!

287
00:14:49,926 --> 00:14:50,968
Move!

288
00:14:52,095 --> 00:14:53,137
I said move!

289
00:14:55,014 --> 00:14:56,057
Shut up!

290
00:14:56,224 --> 00:14:57,850
Okay. Three with me through
the front door.

291
00:14:57,975 --> 00:14:59,519
The rest of you, hit the fire exit
round back.

292
00:14:59,644 --> 00:15:02,605
You start a shooting gallery in there,
and people are gonna get killed.

293
00:15:02,939 --> 00:15:06,025
- See you when we're done.
- CBI has authority here.

294
00:15:06,818 --> 00:15:08,945
I will start arresting your men
and putting them in cuffs

295
00:15:09,070 --> 00:15:10,863
if you don't stand down right now.

296
00:15:11,739 --> 00:15:13,032
Chief, come on!

297
00:15:14,617 --> 00:15:16,494
No, she's right.

298
00:15:17,412 --> 00:15:19,038
CBI has jurisdiction...

299
00:15:19,705 --> 00:15:20,748
for now.

300
00:15:25,002 --> 00:15:26,045
You.

301
00:15:26,504 --> 00:15:27,547
What's your name?

302
00:15:27,922 --> 00:15:29,382
- Donna.
- Donna?

303
00:15:30,007 --> 00:15:31,509
You look familiar. You a D.A.?

304
00:15:31,968 --> 00:15:33,052
I'm a paralegal.

305
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:36,722
Jane, right?

306
00:15:37,223 --> 00:15:38,599
CBI? What are you doing here?

307
00:15:38,891 --> 00:15:41,477
Nothing. In fact, I was just...
I was just leaving.

308
00:15:42,311 --> 00:15:44,605
I just heard on my police scanner
that you guys were looking to arrest me.

309
00:15:45,064 --> 00:15:46,899
You people thought all along
that I killed Amber, didn't you?

310
00:15:47,024 --> 00:15:48,693
What I thought is irrelevant now.

311
00:15:49,277 --> 00:15:53,030
But how exactly is this gun-waving
supposed to establish your innocence?

312
00:15:53,281 --> 00:15:56,117
Oh, I tried talking, it doesn't work.
Nobody listens.

313
00:15:57,910 --> 00:15:58,953
Mind if I get that?

314
00:16:03,749 --> 00:16:04,792
Hello?

315
00:16:05,168 --> 00:16:07,086
Jane? Are you in City Hall?

316
00:16:07,628 --> 00:16:08,754
Yes, unfortunately.

317
00:16:09,172 --> 00:16:10,214
Is anybody hurt?

318
00:16:10,715 --> 00:16:13,384
- Not mortally, yet.
- "What's going on?"

319
00:16:13,676 --> 00:16:15,470
I'd love to chat with you, Lisbon,
but there's a man here

320
00:16:15,595 --> 00:16:17,013
with a large gun,
who wants to talk to you.

321
00:16:19,974 --> 00:16:21,017
Who's this?

322
00:16:21,225 --> 00:16:24,353
Mr. Crosswhite, this is Agent Lisbon.
Let's just take it easy, okay?

323
00:16:24,479 --> 00:16:26,272
You tell all those cops
to stay outta here.

324
00:16:26,731 --> 00:16:29,901
I will. Why are you doing this,
Mr. Crosswhite?

325
00:16:30,026 --> 00:16:31,861
Why, why am I doing this?
Why are you doing this?

326
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:34,655
I'm not doing anything
but talking to you.

327
00:16:35,573 --> 00:16:36,616
What do you want?

328
00:16:36,741 --> 00:16:38,826
I want a guarantee from the governor

329
00:16:39,243 --> 00:16:41,787
and the State Attorney General
that I will not be prosecuted

330
00:16:41,996 --> 00:16:43,247
for the death of Amber Sutherland.

331
00:16:43,581 --> 00:16:44,916
We can talk about that.

332
00:16:45,374 --> 00:16:46,417
And I want...

333
00:16:46,542 --> 00:16:49,045
I want a new investigation
into my wife's death

334
00:16:49,629 --> 00:16:51,088
"and I want the real killer found."

335
00:16:52,131 --> 00:16:53,174
Do it now.

336
00:16:55,218 --> 00:16:56,844
I had two months left on that plan.

337
00:16:58,971 --> 00:17:00,431
May have found a way to hear
what's going on in there.

338
00:17:00,556 --> 00:17:02,558
If we can patch into the main
switchboard for City Hall

339
00:17:02,725 --> 00:17:04,685
we can turn any phone with a speaker
on it into a microphone.

340
00:17:04,810 --> 00:17:05,895
Do it. Where's Nail?

341
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:08,105
He's taken over the cafe on the corner
for a command center.

342
00:17:13,694 --> 00:17:15,530
Nail's tapped into the cameras
around City Hall.

343
00:17:21,494 --> 00:17:23,746
- It's clever.
- Well, just trying to keep up.

344
00:17:23,955 --> 00:17:25,498
It's the rear entrance to City Hall.

345
00:17:25,623 --> 00:17:27,458
It's alarmed, but we can
disarm it from here.

346
00:17:28,125 --> 00:17:30,878
We create a distraction
in front, send men in that way

347
00:17:31,003 --> 00:17:32,421
and we'll minimize casualties.

348
00:17:32,547 --> 00:17:36,300
It's... It's procedure to try and talk the
person who's taken the hostages out.

349
00:17:36,592 --> 00:17:37,677
That's what we're gonna do.

350
00:17:38,135 --> 00:17:40,221
Work with me, Lisbon.
We need a plan B.

351
00:17:40,388 --> 00:17:41,430
Hell with that. Let's go.

352
00:17:41,597 --> 00:17:44,350
We are not going in
unless Crosswhite fires first.

353
00:17:44,517 --> 00:17:46,018
It's the safest path.

354
00:17:46,352 --> 00:17:49,105
Unless you're the first hostage
Crosswhite decides to shoot.

355
00:17:51,691 --> 00:17:53,067
Someone wanna tell me
what's going on?

356
00:17:53,818 --> 00:17:56,320
Mayor Bagshaw, I'm Agent Lisbon
with the CBI.

357
00:17:56,529 --> 00:17:58,614
Glad to hear it.
Nail, what's the plan?

358
00:17:58,906 --> 00:18:00,575
Flashbangs through the side window

359
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,577
move in through the back,
take Crosswhite out.

360
00:18:03,327 --> 00:18:04,870
- Get started on it.
- An assault like that

361
00:18:04,996 --> 00:18:07,248
should be
the last resort, not the first.

362
00:18:08,416 --> 00:18:10,876
A half-dozen people, including my wife

363
00:18:11,127 --> 00:18:13,004
are in that building
with an armed lunatic.

364
00:18:13,212 --> 00:18:14,255
I want them out.

365
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:17,300
I won't allow it.
CBI has the authority here.

366
00:18:18,509 --> 00:18:20,177
Not anymore.
You're to work with us now.

367
00:18:20,886 --> 00:18:24,223
If you don't believe me, talk to your boss.
I already did.

368
00:18:32,523 --> 00:18:36,819
Lisbon, it's a matter of taking
the feelings of the locals into account.

369
00:18:37,194 --> 00:18:39,614
Sir, this is a matter
of people not getting killed.

370
00:18:40,197 --> 00:18:42,199
"You'll do your best
to prevent that, I trust."

371
00:18:42,366 --> 00:18:44,160
I can't if I don't have the authority.

372
00:18:44,327 --> 00:18:46,621
Now I know mayor Bagshaw
has a lot of influence, but...

373
00:18:46,746 --> 00:18:51,208
No, there's no "but." All right?
Influence has influence.

374
00:18:51,375 --> 00:18:53,753
I don't have to explain the politics
of this to you, do I?

375
00:18:54,086 --> 00:18:55,880
Sir, this isn't about politics.

376
00:18:56,047 --> 00:18:58,174
Everything's politics, Lisbon...

377
00:18:58,758 --> 00:18:59,967
"One way or another."

378
00:19:00,801 --> 00:19:03,554
Try persuasion. Works wonders.

379
00:19:12,313 --> 00:19:13,356
What's the word?

380
00:19:13,731 --> 00:19:15,650
- We're on our own.
- No, you don't want them going in.

381
00:19:15,775 --> 00:19:17,151
We better do something.
They're saddling up.

382
00:19:17,485 --> 00:19:18,819
Teresa, I know you're busy

383
00:19:18,944 --> 00:19:20,613
but I'm babysitting a bunch
of reporters out there

384
00:19:20,738 --> 00:19:21,947
who'll take a minute
whenever you've got one.

385
00:19:22,073 --> 00:19:24,909
- Not now, Brenda.
- Fine. Uh, let me know when you can.

386
00:19:26,202 --> 00:19:27,244
Wait a minute.

387
00:19:27,870 --> 00:19:29,038
One. Now.

388
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:32,541
Great. Uh, anyone in particular?
Or should I just pick somebody?

389
00:19:32,917 --> 00:19:35,503
Who do you think has the best access
to director Bertram?

390
00:19:43,552 --> 00:19:46,347
We're human beings.
We have a right to use the bathroom.

391
00:19:48,057 --> 00:19:50,726
There's one in the mayor's office
just right around that corner.

392
00:19:58,442 --> 00:20:00,277
Hey, you're one of those cops
from outta town, right?

393
00:20:03,823 --> 00:20:06,200
Uh, something like that, yeah.

394
00:20:07,410 --> 00:20:09,453
Are you, like, working on a plan
to get us outta this?

395
00:20:09,578 --> 00:20:10,746
Yes. Of course I am.

396
00:20:11,872 --> 00:20:12,915
What are you doing?

397
00:20:15,292 --> 00:20:17,753
Well, I'm... I'm thinking.
And waiting.

398
00:20:20,548 --> 00:20:22,800
What are you, like, 5?
A little patience here.

399
00:20:40,443 --> 00:20:41,777
They're gonna come in, you know.

400
00:20:42,278 --> 00:20:43,696
And it's gonna get all shooty.

401
00:20:44,196 --> 00:20:45,448
What's that gonna prove?

402
00:20:47,908 --> 00:20:49,368
You know what?
Don't put this on me.

403
00:20:51,412 --> 00:20:52,621
You're like all the rest of them.

404
00:20:53,247 --> 00:20:54,957
You just decided I killed Amber.

405
00:20:55,541 --> 00:20:57,710
S-same way they just decided
I killed my wife.

406
00:20:57,835 --> 00:21:00,254
Well, more times than not
it is the husband that did it.

407
00:21:00,421 --> 00:21:01,464
Yeah, well, I didn't.

408
00:21:02,089 --> 00:21:03,841
There were break-ins
all around the neighborhood.

409
00:21:04,008 --> 00:21:06,010
This was a robbery gone wrong.

410
00:21:06,802 --> 00:21:09,430
I, I mean, just because some camera
says I was someplace when I wasn't.

411
00:21:09,555 --> 00:21:12,516
No, they didn't even bother
to, to, to look into the robberies.

412
00:21:12,725 --> 00:21:13,768
That's not true.

413
00:21:15,811 --> 00:21:16,854
What did you say?

414
00:21:17,188 --> 00:21:20,399
We looked into those break-ins.
It was just kids.

415
00:21:21,150 --> 00:21:23,402
They turned on each other
the moment they got arrested.

416
00:21:23,527 --> 00:21:25,070
- They're not killers.
- Donna...

417
00:21:26,197 --> 00:21:27,865
You said you weren't
in the D.A.'s office.

418
00:21:28,157 --> 00:21:30,284
No, I-I just said I was a paralegal.

419
00:21:30,493 --> 00:21:31,619
Somebody killed my wife

420
00:21:31,744 --> 00:21:33,454
and you were too busy
blaming me to catch them.

421
00:21:33,579 --> 00:21:36,332
I-I-I'm sorry I said anything.
Please...

422
00:21:36,499 --> 00:21:39,001
- Please don't shoot me.
- I'm not gonna shoot you. I...

423
00:21:39,126 --> 00:21:41,295
Well, waving the gun in her face
is not a great idea.

424
00:21:41,462 --> 00:21:42,755
Everybody just needs to shut up!

425
00:21:46,383 --> 00:21:49,470
Look, I'm sorry, all right?
I'm sorry. Just please...

426
00:21:51,138 --> 00:21:52,181
Just stop it.

427
00:21:56,727 --> 00:21:57,770
I can help her.

428
00:21:58,979 --> 00:22:00,022
Yeah, please.

429
00:22:03,734 --> 00:22:04,777
It's okay.

430
00:22:06,612 --> 00:22:10,533
It's okay. It's okay.
Just stand up. Breathe.

431
00:22:12,701 --> 00:22:14,161
Just come over here and take a seat.

432
00:22:18,332 --> 00:22:19,583
You know the breath is the switch

433
00:22:19,708 --> 00:22:22,044
between the conscious
and the subconscious mind?

434
00:22:23,003 --> 00:22:24,463
It's how one controls the other.

435
00:22:25,214 --> 00:22:26,257
Just breathe.

436
00:22:29,260 --> 00:22:31,595
Just breathe and relax.

437
00:22:33,389 --> 00:22:35,349
Boss, we've tapped
into the phones at City Hall.

438
00:22:35,474 --> 00:22:36,892
You're gonna wanna hear this.

439
00:22:39,854 --> 00:22:41,397
- Lisbon.
- "Agent Lisbon."

440
00:22:42,314 --> 00:22:45,901
"I, I just had a conversation
with... with a reporter from the Examiner."

441
00:22:46,026 --> 00:22:49,864
He seemed to know a lot
about the situation in Crane Creek.

442
00:22:51,365 --> 00:22:52,867
Now, I told him

443
00:22:53,284 --> 00:22:57,288
that no matter what any
unnamed source might say

444
00:22:57,621 --> 00:23:01,834
"CBI puts civilian safety first
and that we were not bowing"

445
00:23:02,001 --> 00:23:04,003
"to local pressure to do otherwise."

446
00:23:04,837 --> 00:23:08,048
I also told him
that authority in Crane Creek

447
00:23:08,173 --> 00:23:10,217
resides with our head agent
in the field.

448
00:23:10,968 --> 00:23:12,011
You.

449
00:23:12,595 --> 00:23:15,556
"I've let Bagshaw and his chief
know that you're in charge."

450
00:23:15,973 --> 00:23:17,016
Thank you, sir.

451
00:23:18,142 --> 00:23:19,351
We'll discuss this again.

452
00:23:21,145 --> 00:23:22,229
Good luck, Agent.

453
00:23:26,984 --> 00:23:28,152
"In..."

454
00:23:30,779 --> 00:23:31,864
"Out."

455
00:23:32,489 --> 00:23:34,241
"That's good. In..."

456
00:23:35,159 --> 00:23:37,161
"Letting yourself relax."

457
00:23:37,912 --> 00:23:41,123
- "In and out. Just relaxing."
- What's he playing at?

458
00:23:41,832 --> 00:23:43,876
- Sound like he's hypnotizing someone.
- "All the way."

459
00:23:44,627 --> 00:23:48,213
- "Breathing in and out."
- Sir, we're ready to go.

460
00:23:49,632 --> 00:23:53,177
Stand down. No assault
unless Crosswhite starts shooting.

461
00:23:54,011 --> 00:23:56,931
- Agent Lisbon is in charge.
- This is ridiculous.

462
00:23:57,264 --> 00:23:58,307
It's done.

463
00:23:59,183 --> 00:24:00,392
Get back to your post.

464
00:24:01,685 --> 00:24:03,729
"Relaxing your body..."

465
00:24:04,355 --> 00:24:05,564
In...

466
00:24:06,315 --> 00:24:07,816
And out.

467
00:24:08,442 --> 00:24:10,486
Relaxing your body.

468
00:24:11,278 --> 00:24:13,238
Let your eyes close.

469
00:24:14,740 --> 00:24:17,368
That's good. That's good.

470
00:24:19,745 --> 00:24:22,247
Your mind is in fight-or-flight mode.

471
00:24:22,915 --> 00:24:24,416
There's nothing you can do
about that now

472
00:24:24,541 --> 00:24:26,460
so just breathe in...

473
00:24:27,795 --> 00:24:31,382
And out. Let it all fall away...

474
00:24:32,716 --> 00:24:34,426
Fall into the floor.

475
00:24:36,345 --> 00:24:37,805
Now, see yourself...

476
00:24:39,306 --> 00:24:41,058
in a warm, safe place.

477
00:25:05,165 --> 00:25:09,294
In... and out.

478
00:25:11,922 --> 00:25:13,215
Now you're drifting.

479
00:25:19,388 --> 00:25:21,724
Just drifting away.

480
00:25:26,395 --> 00:25:27,438
Oh, my God!

481
00:25:30,315 --> 00:25:32,151
- Oh, my God!
- They tried to kill me.

482
00:25:34,028 --> 00:25:35,237
They tried to kill me.

483
00:25:42,492 --> 00:25:45,787
Sons of bitches. They tried to kill me.

484
00:25:46,955 --> 00:25:47,998
They tried to kill me.

485
00:25:49,082 --> 00:25:51,793
Close the blinds! Go!

486
00:26:02,721 --> 00:26:04,973
Stand down!
Do not fire!

487
00:26:05,348 --> 00:26:06,600
Do not fire!

488
00:26:08,810 --> 00:26:09,853
There he is.

489
00:26:10,103 --> 00:26:11,146
Stop!

490
00:26:13,940 --> 00:26:16,443
Stop! On the ground! Get on the ground!

491
00:26:16,568 --> 00:26:18,153
Face down! Do it now!

492
00:26:22,407 --> 00:26:23,450
Gimme your hands.

493
00:26:31,625 --> 00:26:32,667
Well, what now?

494
00:26:33,543 --> 00:26:34,586
You got me.

495
00:26:39,549 --> 00:26:40,842
You could answer the phone.

496
00:26:51,728 --> 00:26:53,897
Well, that's gonna make it
a little tricky to talk to 'em.

497
00:27:00,028 --> 00:27:01,154
You're gonna talk to them.

498
00:27:03,073 --> 00:27:04,241
I'll tell you what to say.

499
00:27:09,579 --> 00:27:10,622
Okay.

500
00:27:13,542 --> 00:27:15,085
I wanna take Donna with me.
She's hurt.

501
00:27:15,210 --> 00:27:16,711
- She needs he...
- No.

502
00:27:19,923 --> 00:27:21,424
We're gonna book you
for attempted murder.

503
00:27:21,550 --> 00:27:23,718
Call your lawyer,
your union rep, I don't care.

504
00:27:26,138 --> 00:27:27,889
I'm the reason
that Sutherland girl's dead.

505
00:27:28,849 --> 00:27:30,725
- I wanted to make it right.
- Cho, get him outta here.

506
00:27:30,851 --> 00:27:31,893
Come on.

507
00:27:32,435 --> 00:27:34,437
- Boss...
- Yeah, I know. We lost the phones inside.

508
00:27:34,604 --> 00:27:35,647
No, no, no.

509
00:27:36,773 --> 00:27:37,816
It's Jane.

510
00:27:41,987 --> 00:27:43,029
Don't shoot me.

511
00:27:50,120 --> 00:27:52,539
Oh, Lisbon. Nice of you to show up.

512
00:27:52,956 --> 00:27:53,999
Jane?

513
00:27:54,249 --> 00:27:56,376
You know, you people oughta
be ashamed of yourselves.

514
00:27:56,585 --> 00:27:59,004
Crosswhite hasn't shot anyone,
and you've shot Donna.

515
00:27:59,504 --> 00:28:00,547
Is she all right?

516
00:28:01,047 --> 00:28:04,718
Uh, for a shot person, yeah.
She's fine. It's just a graze.

517
00:28:04,926 --> 00:28:07,179
Well, that was sergeant Rowley,
acting on his own.

518
00:28:07,596 --> 00:28:08,638
Says you.

519
00:28:09,014 --> 00:28:11,016
Look, Rowley's screwups
have cost me enough.

520
00:28:11,308 --> 00:28:13,143
If it wasn't for him,
none of us would be here.

521
00:28:13,977 --> 00:28:15,854
You're angry?
How do you think he feels?

522
00:28:16,062 --> 00:28:17,522
Don't start to sympathize with him.

523
00:28:17,647 --> 00:28:19,065
Who is Ronald Crosswhite?

524
00:28:19,649 --> 00:28:21,109
He's a man that no one
has listened to

525
00:28:21,234 --> 00:28:23,236
a man that has been abused
and pushed around.

526
00:28:23,361 --> 00:28:26,907
It's hard not to sympathize
with the man. I do. I feel for him.

527
00:28:27,073 --> 00:28:29,242
Damn it! This isn't a therapy session!

528
00:28:29,492 --> 00:28:32,037
No, it's not. He says you got one hour
to put him in touch

529
00:28:32,162 --> 00:28:33,538
with the governor
and the Attorney General

530
00:28:33,663 --> 00:28:35,040
or he starts shooting hostages.

531
00:28:35,207 --> 00:28:37,459
We'll get on that.
In the meantime could you ask him

532
00:28:37,584 --> 00:28:39,628
to please release
the injured woman?

533
00:28:41,046 --> 00:28:42,214
I never thought of that.

534
00:28:42,672 --> 00:28:43,840
That's a great idea.

535
00:28:53,725 --> 00:28:54,851
Not bad, CBI.

536
00:29:01,399 --> 00:29:02,734
Tell me you didn't kill your wife.

537
00:29:04,736 --> 00:29:05,904
I didn't kill my wife.

538
00:29:07,364 --> 00:29:09,032
- You cheat on her?
- No.

539
00:29:10,659 --> 00:29:12,244
You kept some secret from her.

540
00:29:12,786 --> 00:29:13,828
No.

541
00:29:14,287 --> 00:29:15,622
Yes. There's something.

542
00:29:16,373 --> 00:29:17,958
You just thought about it.
What was it?

543
00:29:21,211 --> 00:29:22,254
I...

544
00:29:24,005 --> 00:29:25,298
I-I was a smoker.

545
00:29:25,799 --> 00:29:28,885
She hated it.
You told her you quit, but you hadn't.

546
00:29:31,972 --> 00:29:33,014
What did you do?

547
00:29:34,182 --> 00:29:35,225
I...

548
00:29:35,809 --> 00:29:38,561
went for long drives,
uh, clear my head...

549
00:29:39,354 --> 00:29:41,523
Snuck a smoke, figured
what's the big deal, right?

550
00:29:41,982 --> 00:29:43,650
That's what you were doing
the night she died.

551
00:29:46,111 --> 00:29:48,571
Uh, I went for a drive,
I listened to some music

552
00:29:49,072 --> 00:29:50,365
had a few smokes.

553
00:29:53,410 --> 00:29:54,744
Came home, she was on the ground.

554
00:29:55,954 --> 00:29:56,997
There was blood.

555
00:29:59,833 --> 00:30:02,711
Put my hands to my face,
smelled the smoke on my fingers.

556
00:30:10,510 --> 00:30:12,262
The last thing I told her was a lie.

557
00:30:14,514 --> 00:30:16,474
And that's the guilt you carry around.

558
00:30:17,309 --> 00:30:18,393
I shoulda been there.

559
00:30:20,061 --> 00:30:21,938
I shoulda been there with her.

560
00:30:22,647 --> 00:30:25,650
Have you ever considered that the killer
was waiting for you to leave?

561
00:30:28,611 --> 00:30:29,654
Does that mean you believe me?

562
00:30:30,238 --> 00:30:31,448
Sure, I guess.

563
00:30:33,074 --> 00:30:36,494
But taking us hostage to prove it
is the dumbest idea you've ever had.

564
00:30:37,537 --> 00:30:38,580
Donna...

565
00:30:38,997 --> 00:30:40,373
The security camera footage

566
00:30:40,498 --> 00:30:42,709
the big evidence
against Mr. Crosswhite

567
00:30:42,834 --> 00:30:45,337
- who owned it?
- Uh, the el-electric company.

568
00:30:45,795 --> 00:30:48,590
Perfect. And Rowley's mistake,
the one that got it thrown out...

569
00:30:49,716 --> 00:30:51,509
Pretty stupid?
Hard to anticipate?

570
00:30:52,344 --> 00:30:54,179
Of all the paperwork to forget

571
00:30:54,596 --> 00:30:55,930
Rowley picked the worst.

572
00:30:56,806 --> 00:30:57,849
That'll do.

573
00:30:58,475 --> 00:31:00,393
Crosswhite, forget about the deadline.

574
00:31:01,019 --> 00:31:03,063
I will tell you who murdered
your wife in 20 minutes.

575
00:31:03,229 --> 00:31:05,357
- I just need three things.
- What?

576
00:31:05,899 --> 00:31:08,109
First, Donna here is injured.

577
00:31:08,234 --> 00:31:09,903
Let her go so she can be taken care of.

578
00:31:10,028 --> 00:31:12,322
There's plenty of us here to shoot
if that's what you feel like doing.

579
00:31:12,447 --> 00:31:13,490
Hey, wha...

580
00:31:13,615 --> 00:31:15,617
Second, I need to go to the bathroom.

581
00:31:15,742 --> 00:31:16,868
- Oh, me, too.
- And me.

582
00:31:18,119 --> 00:31:20,538
- Fine.
- We all get to go to the bathroom.

583
00:31:20,663 --> 00:31:23,041
And third, I need a pen
and some paper.

584
00:31:23,625 --> 00:31:25,293
That's all you need to find
my wife's killer?

585
00:31:26,211 --> 00:31:28,254
Yeah. You think the governor
can say that?

586
00:31:28,671 --> 00:31:29,714
I doubt it.

587
00:31:30,090 --> 00:31:31,132
Okay.

588
00:31:52,278 --> 00:31:54,906
- "You okay to walk?"
- Oh, I'm fine. Fine.

589
00:31:55,198 --> 00:31:57,367
- Tell Kenyon that I'm okay. Tell him...
- No messages.

590
00:31:58,076 --> 00:31:59,119
Go ahead. Open her up.

591
00:32:03,706 --> 00:32:04,749
Donna.

592
00:32:05,208 --> 00:32:07,293
Donna. So brave. Oh, so...

593
00:32:07,419 --> 00:32:10,463
- Ow! Ooh! Ooh. Ooh.
- Oh! Sorry. Forgot about your...

594
00:32:10,630 --> 00:32:11,673
All right.

595
00:32:13,675 --> 00:32:14,717
My bad.

596
00:32:17,595 --> 00:32:19,806
Did Jane tell you to say anything?
Give you a message?

597
00:32:20,014 --> 00:32:22,142
No. He just gave me a hug.

598
00:32:23,017 --> 00:32:24,060
A hug?

599
00:32:25,562 --> 00:32:26,604
Excuse me.

600
00:32:31,151 --> 00:32:32,485
Jane sent us a note.

601
00:32:36,865 --> 00:32:37,907
What's it say?

602
00:32:38,032 --> 00:32:39,617
"Hey, everybody. Solved the case."

603
00:32:39,784 --> 00:32:42,120
"Saw envelope on mayor's desk
left by Amber."

604
00:32:42,245 --> 00:32:44,122
"Must be what the killer
was looking for."

605
00:32:44,456 --> 00:32:46,875
"Can't get to it right now.
Yours truly, Jane."

606
00:32:47,792 --> 00:32:50,587
"P.S: Lisbon, I'm not paying the ticket."

607
00:32:51,880 --> 00:32:53,214
I don't know what the hell that means

608
00:32:53,673 --> 00:32:55,508
but in ten minutes, the deadline's up.

609
00:32:55,967 --> 00:32:57,760
Crosswhite said he's gonna start
shooting people.

610
00:32:58,970 --> 00:33:00,805
Now, I don't care
what you have on Bertram.

611
00:33:01,264 --> 00:33:04,476
If that psycho hurts my wife,
I will break you.

612
00:33:06,060 --> 00:33:07,479
Your ball game, Lisbon.

613
00:33:13,735 --> 00:33:14,903
So what happens now?

614
00:33:17,655 --> 00:33:20,617
Well, what happens now is,
you and I take a walk outside.

615
00:33:21,159 --> 00:33:23,161
- Are you crazy?
- Easy as pie.

616
00:33:23,536 --> 00:33:25,914
- Uh, they'll shoot me.
- Not if I'm standing next to you.

617
00:33:26,122 --> 00:33:27,457
I won't take that chance.

618
00:33:28,082 --> 00:33:29,834
Well, you can take the walk outside

619
00:33:30,335 --> 00:33:32,712
or you can stay in here and wait
for them to come in shooting.

620
00:33:32,837 --> 00:33:34,923
Personally, I like your chances
out there.

621
00:33:35,173 --> 00:33:38,051
I won't do it. I don't even know
why I'm listening to you.

622
00:33:38,343 --> 00:33:41,179
Because I know what I'm talking about.
You're on the edge, and I've been there.

623
00:33:41,304 --> 00:33:43,598
It's a dark and lonely place,
and I'm telling you

624
00:33:43,848 --> 00:33:45,099
this is the way back.

625
00:33:45,934 --> 00:33:48,019
And more than anything else,
I'm offering you what you want...

626
00:33:48,144 --> 00:33:50,939
Your wife's killer
standing in front of you in chains.

627
00:33:51,147 --> 00:33:53,650
Now, if you go out there
there's a chance that you will see that

628
00:33:53,775 --> 00:33:55,860
but if you stay in here
you will probably die.

629
00:33:56,194 --> 00:33:57,237
This is just a trick.

630
00:33:57,445 --> 00:34:00,865
Oh, I wish. If this was a trick,
I'd be a lot more confident.

631
00:34:01,241 --> 00:34:03,201
This is 60/40 at best.

632
00:34:03,993 --> 00:34:07,080
But what's plan B, huh?
You coming?

633
00:34:32,272 --> 00:34:33,815
Oh, that's a lotta guns.

634
00:34:41,153 --> 00:34:43,447
Drop your weapon now!

635
00:34:47,660 --> 00:34:49,912
You get Crosswhite.
We'll get the hostages out.

636
00:34:50,288 --> 00:34:52,456
On your belly! Hands by your sides!

637
00:34:52,623 --> 00:34:54,458
Spread your legs and don't move!

638
00:34:56,586 --> 00:34:57,712
"Go, go, go!"

639
00:35:03,050 --> 00:35:04,635
- You all right?
- Right as rain.

640
00:35:04,927 --> 00:35:05,970
Get your hands back on the back.

641
00:35:06,679 --> 00:35:08,097
- Now!
- Easy, Rigsby.

642
00:35:09,390 --> 00:35:10,433
Easy.

643
00:35:17,481 --> 00:35:18,524
Jessica!

644
00:35:36,459 --> 00:35:37,877
Well, looks like you had it wrong.

645
00:35:38,586 --> 00:35:40,421
There was no envelope
on the mayor's desk.

646
00:35:41,255 --> 00:35:42,340
You're gonna wanna see this.

647
00:35:43,257 --> 00:35:45,593
There's nothing there
because you have it stuffed

648
00:35:45,760 --> 00:35:47,887
inside your bulletproof vest.

649
00:35:49,347 --> 00:35:51,515
- Excuse me?
- He killed Ginger Crosswhite

650
00:35:51,724 --> 00:35:53,392
and he killed Amber Sutherland.

651
00:35:56,270 --> 00:35:57,313
Arnold?

652
00:35:57,772 --> 00:36:00,441
What possible reason could I have
to hurt those women?

653
00:36:00,733 --> 00:36:03,069
Well, Ginger, I'm not so sure about yet,
but Amber...

654
00:36:03,611 --> 00:36:04,779
she found out, didn't she?

655
00:36:05,655 --> 00:36:06,906
You got your killer right there.

656
00:36:07,031 --> 00:36:09,492
Yeah, and you were terrified
I was starting to believe him.

657
00:36:09,950 --> 00:36:12,703
If he was telling the truth about what
time he came home that night...

658
00:36:12,870 --> 00:36:15,247
Then the security footage
doesn't make sense.

659
00:36:16,499 --> 00:36:17,541
What do you mean?

660
00:36:17,792 --> 00:36:20,127
Well, it's unlikely the electric
company meddled with it.

661
00:36:20,461 --> 00:36:23,089
You had access to the evidence
and you changed it.

662
00:36:23,339 --> 00:36:25,758
Amber, the video expert, figured it out.

663
00:36:26,717 --> 00:36:27,760
And then you killed her.

664
00:36:28,511 --> 00:36:30,346
But what you didn't know
is she left a message

665
00:36:30,513 --> 00:36:32,640
about what she found
on the mayor's desk.

666
00:36:33,307 --> 00:36:34,642
There was no envelope.

667
00:36:35,935 --> 00:36:36,977
Yes, there was...

668
00:36:38,312 --> 00:36:39,397
'Cause I put it there.

669
00:36:41,399 --> 00:36:42,525
Now let's see it.

670
00:36:48,197 --> 00:36:50,366
Chief Nail, take off your vest.

671
00:37:04,463 --> 00:37:05,506
Open it.

672
00:37:11,220 --> 00:37:12,263
Read it out.

673
00:37:16,058 --> 00:37:17,101
"Arrest me."

674
00:37:19,895 --> 00:37:20,938
Okay.

675
00:37:22,857 --> 00:37:25,401
Look at that, huh?
You don't have to say that twice.

676
00:37:27,570 --> 00:37:29,447
- I'm not going to jail!
- Don't do it! Don't.

677
00:37:31,782 --> 00:37:32,825
Stay down!

678
00:37:34,326 --> 00:37:35,369
That was close.

679
00:37:36,954 --> 00:37:39,832
"We have people looking
at the security footage right now."

680
00:37:40,082 --> 00:37:42,793
It's only a matter of time
before they figure out what you did.

681
00:37:43,627 --> 00:37:45,755
Now you're a cop
about to go into the system.

682
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:47,047
You do the math.

683
00:37:50,301 --> 00:37:52,511
Ginger Crosswhite got herself killed.

684
00:37:54,305 --> 00:37:56,015
I want you to understand that.

685
00:37:58,642 --> 00:38:01,771
"We'd talked at City Hall.
She was not an innocent."

686
00:38:02,396 --> 00:38:04,440
"She married down.
Anybody could see that..."

687
00:38:04,607 --> 00:38:05,733
"I certainly could."

688
00:38:06,192 --> 00:38:08,194
"It was clear as day
that she was unhappy."

689
00:38:08,652 --> 00:38:10,863
"There was a connection
between us."

690
00:38:11,405 --> 00:38:14,116
"Very powerful one.
At least, I felt there was."

691
00:38:16,911 --> 00:38:18,829
"But she was gonna tell the world..."

692
00:38:20,122 --> 00:38:21,499
"Like I assaulted her."

693
00:38:25,586 --> 00:38:26,837
"Defiled..."

694
00:38:29,173 --> 00:38:31,675
Like I was some disgusting...

695
00:38:33,302 --> 00:38:34,345
"thing."

696
00:38:36,388 --> 00:38:38,140
"Where'd you get
the video of Crosswhite?"

697
00:38:40,601 --> 00:38:44,939
"I hacked into the security footage,
changed the time stamp."

698
00:38:46,106 --> 00:38:47,566
I had Crosswhite cold.

699
00:38:48,776 --> 00:38:52,029
And that idiot Rowley forgot
to file the warrant.

700
00:38:52,530 --> 00:38:54,114
So Crosswhite walked...

701
00:38:55,366 --> 00:38:58,786
and lived in a purgatory you created
for him until he met Amber.

702
00:38:59,411 --> 00:39:02,122
And she figured out that there was
something wrong with the footage?

703
00:39:02,665 --> 00:39:06,418
Said the "meta-data" didn't match.

704
00:39:07,086 --> 00:39:09,046
She had no idea I was involved.

705
00:39:10,381 --> 00:39:14,134
And she said that she hadn't told
anyone else, so...

706
00:39:15,636 --> 00:39:16,929
I met her at her home.

707
00:39:35,739 --> 00:39:39,159
And you took her cameras
and you planted one at Crosswhite's.

708
00:39:40,786 --> 00:39:41,954
In for a penny.

709
00:39:46,166 --> 00:39:47,293
I thought that...

710
00:39:49,420 --> 00:39:52,381
When I confessed, I would
feel a weight lift.

711
00:39:56,176 --> 00:39:57,303
I don't feel anything.

712
00:40:02,558 --> 00:40:04,101
Crosswhite.
It's time.

713
00:40:07,521 --> 00:40:08,564
Hey...

714
00:40:09,398 --> 00:40:11,400
Sorry about the whole jail thing

715
00:40:11,775 --> 00:40:13,569
but you did take a bunch
of people hostage.

716
00:40:14,445 --> 00:40:15,487
I don't care.

717
00:40:16,322 --> 00:40:18,032
Jail doesn't mean anything to me now.

718
00:40:19,033 --> 00:40:21,994
Yeah, well, see how you feel
about that in a couple years.

719
00:40:23,412 --> 00:40:24,455
I'll be fine.

720
00:40:25,748 --> 00:40:26,957
I can breathe again.

721
00:40:28,709 --> 00:40:29,752
Thank you.

722
00:40:44,224 --> 00:40:46,310
Are you familiar with the regulations

723
00:40:46,518 --> 00:40:49,730
regarding agents giving anonymous
statements to the press?

724
00:40:51,440 --> 00:40:54,526
CBI employees shall not give
anonymous

725
00:40:54,652 --> 00:40:58,113
or "off the record" statements
to members of the media.

726
00:40:58,530 --> 00:41:01,367
And what are the repercussions
of said violation?

727
00:41:01,909 --> 00:41:04,203
- Suspension or termination.
- Yes.

728
00:41:06,830 --> 00:41:10,376
However, both the Bagshaws are happy.
Everyone's alive.

729
00:41:10,668 --> 00:41:11,710
We caught the killer.

730
00:41:13,963 --> 00:41:15,005
Yes, sir.

731
00:41:16,674 --> 00:41:18,884
See, you, you find the right lever

732
00:41:19,176 --> 00:41:21,553
agent, you can move the world.

733
00:41:23,681 --> 00:41:24,848
You found the right lever.

734
00:41:26,016 --> 00:41:27,726
That was a smart play.

735
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:31,939
I hope you stay smart.

736
00:41:39,613 --> 00:41:40,656
What was that about?

737
00:41:40,781 --> 00:41:43,325
Oh, it was just business.
What's that?

738
00:41:43,701 --> 00:41:46,620
This, this is my speeding ticket
that I refuse to pay.

739
00:41:46,745 --> 00:41:47,830
Well, I'm not paying it.

740
00:41:49,081 --> 00:41:50,499
Well, then I guess no one's gonna pay.

741
00:41:50,749 --> 00:41:52,001
I'll get Bertram to pay it.

742
00:41:52,668 --> 00:41:54,253
- How are you gonna do that?
- I have my ways.

743
00:42:04,596 --> 00:42:05,639
It's on your desk!

